  "title": "Edge-Colouring Geometric Complete Graphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Question What is the minimum number of colours such that every complete geometric graph on $n$ vertices has an edge colouring such that:\n\n\\item[Variant A] crossing edges get distinct colours, \\item[Variant B] disjoint edges get distinct colours, \\item[Variant C] non-disjoint edges get distinct colours, \\item[Variant D] non-crossing edges get distinct colours.",
